    "html": "<p>A small source of thermal radiation has an absolute temperature <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T\"></span>. At a distance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r\"></span> from the source, the intensity of the radiation measured is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I\"></span>. The temperature of the source is increased to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2T\"></span> and the intensity is measured at a distance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2r\"></span> from the source. What is the new intensity measured?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4I\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"8I\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"16I\"></span></p></li></ol>"
